\section{Conclusions}

We have shown that using the thermodynamically consistent Gibbs construction for the first-order phase transition that
occurs in the relativistic mean-field model with $\sigma$--$\delta$ and $\omega$--$\delta$ meson crossing term leads to a thick
neutron crust. The mass--radius relation may be controlled to some extent by the coupling to the $\sigma$ field,
and in a reasonable range of its values, the mass--radius relation is in close agreement with the most reliable observational 
constraints.


