\section{Conclusion}
This paper introduces the \texttt{OpenDPDv2} framework, aiming to streamline DPD model learning, optimization, and standard datasets for better simulation. The \texttt{OpenDPDv2} framework is packed with a new DPD model, \ac{TRes-DeltaGRU}, leveraging quantization and temporal sparsity. Results show proposed FP32 \ac{TRes-DeltaGRU}-996 achieves the state-of-the-art linearization performance with 200\,MHz OFDM signal. By reducing computational complexity and memory access compared to conventional approaches, quantized \ac{TRes-DeltaGRU} achieves a saving of $E_\text{F}$, which helps to bring down the both inference and online adaptation energy consumption of \ac{NN} \ac{DPD}s, while maintaining robust linearization performance.

