\subsection{RQ3: How Does Trust in ChatGPT Vary by Task Type?}

Participants indicated whether they had used ChatGPT for specific tasks. As shown in Figure~\ref{fig:task_freq}, summarising and coding were the most frequent uses, reported by about two-thirds of participants. Other common tasks included explaining, information gathering, proofreading and idea generation, each used by over half the sample. Less frequent uses included translating, entertainment and sourcing references.

