\begin{abstract}
    We present a (semi)-algorithm to compute winning strategies for parametric timed games.
    Previous algorithms only synthesized constraints on the clock parameters for which the game is winning.
    A new definition of (winning) strategies is proposed, and ways to compute them.
    A transformation of these strategies to (parametric) timed automata allows for
    building a controller enforcing them.
    The feasibility of the method is demonstrated by an implementation 
    and experiments
    for the Production Cell case study.
\end{abstract}

