Each image in the plot corresponds to a different class, with the title indicating both the actual label and the predicted label. In cases where the model has correctly predicted the label, we visualise a set of random predictions made by the model, in Figure 14, which include both correct and incorrect classifications. This step provides insight into how well the model generalizes to new data and where it may be making mistakes in distinguishing between classes.

