\section{Experiments}
\subsection{Evaluation Metrics}
As in the SEACells paper \cite{Persad2022.04.02.486748}, we use compactness, separation, and cell-type purity for the metacell benchmark. Compactness measures how homogeneous the cells within a metacell are. Separation assesses how metacells are distinct from each other. Cell-type purity, instead, measures the consistency of cell-types among cells that constitute a metacell.  
We computed diffusion components using principal components from RNA assay (RNA\_PCA) or singular values singular values from ATAC assay (ATAC\_SVD), and then quantified the compactness and separation of metacells.
Since SEACells identifies metacells from one modality, we denote them as SeaC-ATAC and SeaC-RNA.


\subsection{Results}
