\subsection{Short-term and Long-term Driving Factors}
\label{subsec: shor_long_term_factors}

To delve deeper into which individual metrics affect the predictive capabilities of forecasting models, two groups were created based on the final feature vectors. Specifically, features from sets with different prediction windows were merged together to form the \textit{Short-term} (windows 1 and 7) and \textit{Long-term} (windows 90 and 180) groups. Fine-tuned random forests were used to extract an importance value for each feature in the final feature vectors. When creating the groups, the importance of common features within a group was calculated by averaging their importance value before merging. To better understand which individual indicators affect each group and why, their brief definitions are provided in Table \ref{tab:fet_definitions}.

