\begin{proof}[Proof of Proposition~\ref{lemma:stability:aminse}]
The result can be recovered as follows
\begin{align*}
    \prob\ens{Y \notin C_{\hatSxiepsilon}^\alpha(X)} &= \expec\closed{\sum_{i=1}^K \pstarstar{b}{\xi}\one\ens{Y\notin C_{i}^{\alpha'}(X)}}\\
    &\leq \sum_{i=1}^K e^\eta b_i \prob\ens{Y\notin C_{i}^{\alpha'}(X)} +\tau
    \leq e^\eta \alpha' + \tau \leq \alpha,
\end{align*}
where the first and last inequalities follow from the two constraint $d_i\leq {e^\eta}b_i + s_i$ and $e^\eta \alpha' +\tau   \leq  \alpha$ in \ref{eq:AdaMinSE}, respectively. 
