\section{Preliminaries}
\label{sec:prelim}

In this section, we present some basic properties of the multi-species interacting particle system~\eqref{eq: many SDEs}, of the mean-field McKean-Vlasov PDEs~\eqref{eq: multi-species PDE} and of the McKean SDEs~\eqref{eq: mean-field SDE} that will be needed later on. In Section~\ref{subsec:well_posed} we present a basic well-posedness result for the mean-field SDEs; in Section~\ref{subsec:prop_chaos} we present a basic propagation of chaos theorem. In Section~\ref{subsec:stat_states} we characterize all stationary states of the mean-field dynamics. Finally, in Section~\ref{subsec:free_energy} we derive the free-energy of the mean-field system, under the symmetry Assumption~\ref{asp: assumption}, and we  show that it is non-increasing and lower-bounded.

%introduce the material necessary to proceed with our study. Namely, we will justify briefly why the multi-species McKean-Vlasov system is well-posed. Then, we will do the same for the propagation of chaos between this system and the related interacting particles system. In a subsequent subsection, we will give the general form of the invariant probability measures (in term of Gibbs measure). This latter subsection will be crucial to get the so-called self-consistent equations that completely characterizes the stationary states. In a fourth subsection, we will introduce the free-energy functional and we will show that it is non-increasing and lower-bounded, which will be essential to obtain the convergence.
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
\subsection{Well-posedness of the multi-species SDEs}
\label{subsec:well_posed}

We start by stating a basic well-posedness result for the multi-species McKean SDE system.


\begin{theorem}%[Well-posedness of the multi-species SDEs]  
\label{thm: well-posedness}
Suppose that Assumptions \ref{asp: assumption} and \ref{asp: assumptionbis} hold and that the initial conditions $\{X_i(0)\}$ $i=1,\ldots M$ satisfy $\E(|X_i(0)|^{8p^2})<\infty$ where $p>0$ is defined in (H3) of Assumption \ref{asp: assumption}. Then the system \eqref{eq: mean-field SDE} admits a unique strong solution in $\bRb_+$. Furthermore, the $8 p^2$ moments are uniformly bounded in time for any index $k$, with the upper bound depending only on the moments of the initial conditions.
%In other words, given a probability space with $M$ Brownian motions, there exists a solution to the system with these Brownian motions.
\end{theorem}

This theorem is proved for $M=2$ in~\cite[Theorem 2.1]{DuongTugaut2020}. The proof is based on a fixed point theorem on an appropriate function space; see \cite[Definition 2.1]{DuongTugaut2020}. The extension to the $M > 2$ case is immediate, and we omit the details.  We also remark that the theorem can be easily extended to non-quadratic interaction potentials provided that they satisfy a polynomial growth assumption. Theorem~\ref{thm: well-posedness} is sufficient for the purposes of this paper.
