\section{CONCLUSION}
\label{con}
This paper primarily investigates the convergence speed of spatially coupled LDPC ensembles under WD. Specifically, an upper bound on the convergence speed is derived, which can inform the design of the number of iterations required within each decoding window. Simulation results further demonstrate that, under the same channel conditions, ensembles with different degree distributions exhibit varying convergence speeds. This observation suggests the potential for future work aimed at designing degree distributions that optimize convergence speed.

