During transmission, some packets may be lost, but the parity fragments allow the receiver to recover many lost data fragments without retransmission. As illustrated in~\autoref{fig:receive}, for the first level, as long as no more than 4 fragments are lost within each FTG, the data can be fully recovered. Similarly, lost fragments at levels 2 and 3 can be recovered using parity fragments. However, at level 4, if 2 fragments are lost from an FTG, recovery is not possible due to the single parity fragment. If retransmission is not enabled, only the top three levels can be used for reconstruction within error bound $\varepsilon_{3}$. The number of parity fragments at each level can be adjusted based on user requirements.


