\begin{abstract}
% % s1
% Leveraging Large Language Models (LLMs) for recommendation has demonstrated remarkable success in various tasks, showcasing their potential for open-domain recommendation. 
% % s2
% A key challenge to advancing open-domain recommendation lies in effectively modeling user preferences within their heterogeneous behaviors across multiple domains.
% % s3
% Existing approaches, including ID-based and semantic-based modeling, struggle with poor generalization, the domain seesaw phenomenon, and the inability to effectively compress noisy interactions. 
% % s4
% To address these challenges, we propose HUM (Heterogeneous User Modeling), which incorporates  a compression enhancer and a robustness enhancer. 
% % s5
% Compression enhancer employs a designed prompt to compress heterogeneous interactions into a tailored token in LLMs while leveraging a masking mechanism to enhance cross-domain knowledge extraction and understanding.
% % s6
% Robustness enhancer introduces a domain influential score to mitigate the domain seesaw effect by regulating domain optimization. 
% % s7
% Extensive experiments on heterogeneous datasets validate that HUM effectively models user heterogeneity by achieving both strong compression capability and robustness, leading to superior performance in open-domain recommendation. 

% s1
Leveraging Large Language Models (LLMs) for recommendation has demonstrated notable success in various domains, showcasing their potential for open-domain recommendation.
% s2
A key challenge to advancing open-domain recommendation lies in effectively modeling user preferences from users' heterogeneous behaviors across multiple domains.
% s3
Existing approaches, including ID-based and semantic-based modeling, struggle with poor generalization, an inability to compress noisy interactions effectively, and the domain seesaw phenomenon.
% s4
To address these challenges, 
% we propose a method named HUM (Heterogeneous User Modeling), which incorporates a compression enhancer along with a robustness enhancer for LLM-based recommendation.
we propose a Heterogeneous User Modeling (HUM) method, which incorporates a compression enhancer and a robustness enhancer for LLM-based recommendation. 
% s5
The compression enhancer uses a customized prompt to compress heterogeneous behaviors into a tailored token, while a masking mechanism enhances cross-domain knowledge extraction and understanding.
% s6
The robustness enhancer introduces a domain importance score to mitigate the domain seesaw phenomenon by guiding domain optimization. 
% s7
Extensive experiments on heterogeneous datasets validate that HUM effectively models user heterogeneity by achieving both high efficacy and robustness, leading to superior performance in open-domain recommendation.

% \vspace{-0.1cm}
\end{abstract}

