\subsection{NGC~6153}
NGC~6153 displays two prominent LISs at the eastern and western parts of the nebula, as illustrated by the [O~{\sc i}] 6300~$\AA$ line map (Fig.~\ref{ngc6153_append}). We verified the detection of the emission lines [Fe~{\sc iii}]~4881~$\AA$ and 5270~$\AA$, [Fe~{\sc ii}] 7155~$\AA$ and 8617~$\AA$, and [Ni~{\sc ii}] 7378~$\AA$ and [C~{\sc i}] 8727~$\AA$ (Fig.~\ref{ngc6153_text}). [Fe~{\sc ii}] 8617~$\AA$ and [Ni~{\sc ii}] 7378~$\AA$ lines are found to emanate from the same regions, while [Fe~{\sc iii}] 5270~$\AA$ comes from two district regions with different orientation.
