Similarly to the case of NGC~3242, a spatial offset between the [Fe~{\sc ii}] 8617~$\AA$ and [C~{\sc i}] 8727~$\AA$ lines have been found in the outer pair of LIS as well as the northern clump. In particular, the peak of [Fe~{\sc ii}] 8617~$\AA$ is located 0.4\arcsec~closer to the central star in the E LIS (K1), and 0.5\arcsec~further away in the northern clump (see Fig.~\ref{ngc7009_contours}). As mentioned in Sect. \ref{sec_3242}, additional observations are needed in order to clarify whether ionization stratification or dynamical effects are responsible for this offset.

