\abstract{
We present the full Hamiltonian analysis of electrodynamics, including fermions, photons, and their interaction, on a general curved spacetime in Ashtekar-Barbero variables. No gauge fixing is performed and the theory is background independent. The details of the constraints of the theory for both Weyl and Dirac fermions are presented. Moreover, the equations of motion are derived and it is shown that they reduce to the equations of motion of the standard QFT in curved or flat spacetime in the appropriate limits. Finally, the behavior of the theory under parity transformation is analyzed.
}
